ue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.3 and 4.4beta3.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 - Vulkan - Godot 4.3 stable and 4.4beta3 (and all the betas I bet)\n\n### Issue description\n\nVoxelGI \"No data\" warning is sticky and only seems to refresh/recalculate when the scene tree is updated, with slight differences--explained in repro steps--between 4.3 and 4.4b due to scene graph editor optimizations.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRepro steps for 4.3:\n* Make a new VoxelGI node\n* The \"no data\" warning appears (correctly)\n* Create a new data node (doesn't matter if it's scene local or saved)\n* The \"no data\" warning STAYS (incorrectly! we have data set!)\n* Nothing you do within the node itself will make the warning go away.\n* Re-arrange the node tree in any way (ie: change unrelated nodes positions in the tree) and the warning will recompute and go away.\n\nRepro steps for 4.4b3:\n* Same as above EXCEPT the warning only goes away when the VoxelGI node itself is affected. Likely due to recent optimizations in the scene graph handling (postulated in rocket chat discussion [here](https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/rendering?msg=Gb5fbB9kS1nATWWg9))\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMRP not included because you can do this for yourself in like 10 clicks.","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":